# Certifying that a program computes `size`: given a tree, does it return the
# node count of its argument, as an Snat, on every input?
#
# In tree calculus a program is a tree, and so is its data, so a checker can
# read the program it is handed instead of trusting the toolchain behind it.
# [computes_size] evaluates the program on a symbolic tree and discharges the
# result by structural induction, so a verdict covers all inputs rather than
# the ones a test enumerates.
#
# A goal pairs a symbolic term with what it must evaluate to, written in an
# abstract Snat: a multiset of `1`s, `|t|`s (the size of tree variable t) and
# `n`s (the value of an Snat variable). The top goal is `p t ⊨ |t|`. Five rules
# close it, each either a fact about trees or a step of the induction — the
# lazy certifier further down extends them with seven more, rendered at its
# own header:
#   • NORMALIZE  reduce the term symbolically, on a budget; opaque variables
#                block reduction and the evaluator reports the one it waits on
#   • PEEL       a term that reduced to `△ x` is a successor, so spend a `1`
#                from the spec and continue with `x`
#   • SPLIT      case on the blocking variable — every tree is △, △a or △ab and
#                every Snat is △ or △n, so the cases are exhaustive; the spec is
#                updated by the defining equations of size. The goal split here
#                becomes an induction hypothesis, reusable only on a variable
#                the split created.
#   • FOLD       a goal that is an instance of such a hypothesis is closed by
#                it. The instance must map the split variable strictly below
#                itself — to a part the split produced, or to a variable
#                GEN-TREE minted from disjoint proper parts — so the node
#                count strictly decreases: that is the well-founded measure
#                the induction rests on.
#   • GENERALIZE a subterm a hypothesis proves is a known Snat becomes a fresh
#                Snat variable, and its share of the spec goes with it. Without
#                it the analysis chases an unbounded family of accumulator
#                states; with it, the state space is finite.
#
# [computes_size_eagerly]'s prover has four rules of its own, added for the
# programs whose recursion is not on a subtree of the input:
#   • RGEN       a literal △ in argument position down the state's spine — an
#                accumulator seed — becomes an opaque residual r, and the spec
#                gains the atom ⟨r⟩, "then the tree r": a state owing E ⊎ [⟨r⟩]
#                evaluates to r under sum(E) successors. The hypothesis the
#                next split records then covers every accumulator, and r := △
#                recovers the plain goal, a stack over a leaf being an Snat.
#   • GEN-TREE   a subterm a hypothesis proves evaluates to a known-size chain
#                — part sizes stacked over a residual — becomes a fresh tree
#                variable of exactly that size, its parts recorded in its name
#                for FOLD's measure check. A machine that emits its successors
#                outside the loop hands the chain on without its head
#                constructor, so the hypothesis is also tried one synthesized
#                stem up, the missing node returning to the spec as a 1. This
#                is what closes recursion on rebuilt trees — the chain step of
#                Snat.size__103 among them — where structural FOLD
#                cannot.
#   • REL-FOLD   FOLD widened to a goal that is no instance of any
#                hypothesis: an instance strictly below closes it anyway if
#                the two states co-reduce apart by exactly what is left of
#                the spec — the difference is proven, not matched.
#   • REL-USE    inside that co-reduction, a machine handed its own loop
#                value as its accumulator is collapsed to that value's
#                continuation, one size atom paid. An opaque residual blocks
#                a step that reads its accumulator's shape; this rule rides
#                it instead, and is what certifies the record pair — the 78
#                and the 90, whose fork case is self u self v k. Both are
#                spelled out at their definitions below, and shared with the
#                lazy prover.
#
# Generalization is what makes the certificate style-agnostic: `1+(|a|+|b|)` and
# an accumulator threaded through the traversal reduce differently, and both
# close, because the arithmetic is done by the abstract Snat rather than by
# matching one program's shape against another's.
#
# This does not decide `size` — Rice's theorem forbids that. Passing guarantees
# the program is `size` on all inputs; failing means "no proof within the search
# bounds". The analysis is an underapproximation by design: it gives up beyond
# `_depth` nested case splits, and when the accumulated state never folds, as in
# `compose Snat.from_nat size` — that is `size`, but it counts in binary Nat and
# converts at the end, so the induction never closes over the unary spec.
#
# NORMALIZE runs on a budget, so a term with no normal form costs a fallback
# rather than an answer that never comes. The `__wn` programs in
# src/snat/size.lamb are the ones that spend it: their recursion unfolds under
# the constructor it emits, so their states have no normal form at all — head
# reduction returns, normalizing what it returns does not, and the head is
# what NORMALIZE hands the rules. The lazy certifier's three extensions are
# what close an induction over such heads.
#
# That the budget can be spent at all is what src/quoted/spine.lamb is for. Its
# reduction rewrites the front of an argument list, so what a rule drops is
# dropped as a list element and an eager evaluator never looks inside it —
# where the term-rebuilding [Quoted.eval] makes an eager host pay for every
# term the reduction walks past, which on some of the `__wn` programs is a
# price this repository cannot pay. The analysis is a program here like any
# other, and it has to hold to the same rule as its subject matter.
#
# Which order it diverges under is the other question a reader of a program can
# settle, since tree calculus prescribes none and `size` can be written to
# converge in only one of them — the `__wn` programs are exactly that, and
# smaller for it. NORMALIZE is where the difference lives, so it is the only
# thing [computes_size_eagerly] changes: it normalizes both halves of an
# application before letting a rule fire on it, so a rule only ever discards a
# term that is already a normal form. Discarding a normal form discards
# nothing that could have diverged, and discarding is the only way one order
# can converge where another does not, so a program that terminates under this
# order terminates under every one: [p t] strongly normalizes.
#
# That one is on a budget too, of rule applications rather than head
# reductions, and outrunning it is what an eagerly divergent program does — so
# [computes_size_eagerly] answers on everything, which the other one still does
# not. Neither refines the other: each is a verdict the other cannot give.
#
# The tests are next door in test.lamb, which is free to reach into Snat for
# programs to judge. This file is not: Snat's size programs depend on it.

# Symbolic terms. Reflect's quoted encoding doubles as the term language:
#   △ = a leaf, [△ n] = an opaque variable named n, [△ f x] = the application f x
_var = \n △ n
_app = \f \x △ f x

# Names are lists: splitting a variable prefixes a step to its name, so
# [_extends v w] — "w names a part the splitting of v produced" — is exactly
# "v is a proper suffix of w". Fresh Snat variables get one-element names.
_extends = \v fix $ \self triage false (\_ false) (\_ \tl Bool.or (equal tl v) (self tl))
_part = \i \v △ i v
_fresh = \g [g]
_input = _fresh Snat.zero

# The abstract Snat: a multiset of atoms.
_one = △              # a literal successor
_sz = \v △ v          # the size of tree variable v
_val = \v △ △ v       # the value of Snat variable v

# A fourth atom, for the size-measure induction: [△ (△ △) r] is ⟨r⟩, "then
# the tree r" — a state owing E ⊎ [⟨r⟩] must evaluate to the value of r under
# sum(E) successors rather than to a bare Snat. At most one per spec, and the
# plain judgment is the special case ⟨△⟩, a stack of successors over a leaf
# being exactly an Snat. The lazy certifier further down spells its ⟨★k⟩ tail
# the same way but reads it as continuation obligations; the two provers never
# exchange specs, so the encoding is shared and the semantics are not.
_res = \r △ (△ △) r
_atom4 = \o1 \osz \oval \ores triage o1 osz (\c \v triage (oval v) (\_ ores v) (\_ \_ oval v) c)
_res_var = _atom4 Option.none (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none) Option.some
_has_res = \e List.any (\a Option.match false (\_ true) (_res_var a)) e

# Tree variables minted by [_gen_tree] carry their accounting in their name: a
# fork head that no part- or counter-name has, then the list of part variables
# whose sizes the minted tree adds up to. [_below] is FOLD's well-foundedness
# check, widened from "a part the splitting produced" to also accept a minted
# variable whose recorded parts are pairwise disjoint parts strictly below the
# split variable: disjoint proper parts never add up to the whole tree, so the
# node count still strictly decreases and the induction stays well-founded.
_gname = \parts △ (△ △ △) parts
_gparts = triage Option.none (\_ Option.none)
  (\hd \tl triage Option.none (\_ Option.none) (\_ \_ Option.some tl) hd)
_disjoint = fix $ \self List.match true (\hd \tl Bool.and
  (List.all (\o Bool.not (Bool.or (equal hd o) (Bool.or (_extends hd o) (_extends o hd)))) tl)
  (self tl))
_below = \v \w Bool.match
  (Option.match false (\parts Bool.and (Bool.not (List.is_empty parts))
    (Bool.and (List.all (_extends v) parts) (_disjoint parts))) (_gparts w))
  true
  (_extends v w)

_remove = \x fix $ \self List.match Option.none
  (\hd \tl Bool.match (Option.map (△ hd) (self tl)) (Option.some tl) (equal hd x))
_minus = \f \e List.foldl (\acc \x Option.bind (_remove x) acc) (Option.some e) f
_spec_eq = \a \b Option.match false List.is_empty $ _minus a b

# Search combinators that stop at the first answer. List.any and List.all force
# every element under eager reduction, and each element here is a whole subproof;
# these keep the tail under a lambda, so a later element is explored only if the
# earlier ones leave the question open.
_first = \f fix $ \self List.match Option.none
  (\hd \tl Option.match self (\x \_ Option.some x) (f hd) tl)
_all = \f fix $ \self List.match true (\hd \tl Bool.match (\_ false) self (f hd) tl)

# Delay a call until its branch is taken. Eager reduction evaluates an
# application the moment none of its parts is an unbound variable, so a call
# written in an untaken branch still runs while the branch is built — unless
# some argument of every prefix mentions a variable of the branch itself.
# [_at u f] is [f], with u woven in as that variable: [_at u f a b] costs two
# extra rule applications and computes nothing until u is bound.
_at = \u \f f

# First-order matching: pattern variables bind to subterms of the target.
_capture = \n \t \s Option.match
  (Option.some $ △ (△ n t) s)
  (\prev Bool.match Option.none (Option.some s) (equal prev t))
  (List.lookup n s)
_match = fix $ \self \p \t \s triage
  (triage (Option.some s) (\_ Option.none) (\_ \_ Option.none) t)
  (\n _capture n t s)
  (\pf \px triage Option.none (\_ Option.none)
     (\tf \tx Option.match Option.none (\s2 self px tx s2) $ self pf tf s) t)
  p

# Hypotheses: [△ state (△ spec split_variable)].
# The instance must send the split variable strictly below itself; that is the
# measure that makes reuse an induction hypothesis rather than a circular claim.
_image = \s \v Option.bind (triage Option.none (\w Option.some w) (\_ \_ Option.none)) $ List.lookup v s
_rename = \s _atom4 (Option.some _one) (\v Option.map _sz $ _image s v)
  (\v Option.map _val $ _image s v) (\r Option.map _res $ _image s r)
_fold = \a \t Pair.let a $ \state \r Pair.let r $ \spec \v
  Option.bind (\s Option.bind
    (\w Bool.match Option.none (Option.sequence $ List.map (_rename s) spec) $ _below v w)
    (_image s v))
    (_match state t [])

# Generalization: a subterm a hypothesis proves is a known Snat.
_subterms = \t (fix $ \self \t \acc triage acc (\_ acc)
  (\f \x △ f $ self f $ △ x $ self x acc) t) t []
_replace = \needle \v fix $ \self \t
  Bool.match (triage △ (\a △ a) (\f \x △ (self f) (self x)) t) v (equal t needle)
_generalize = \g \asms \e \s
  _first (\c _first (\a Option.bind (\f Option.map
    (\rest △ (_replace c (_var g) s) (△ (_val g) rest)) $ _minus f e) $ _fold a c) asms) (_subterms s)

# Generalization for the size measure: a subterm a hypothesis proves evaluates
# to a known-size chain — its renamed spec is a core of part sizes over ⟨b⟩ —
# becomes a fresh tree variable. The parts and b leave the goal's spec and the
# minted variable's size enters it; the name records the parts for [_below].
_gen_tree = \asms \e \s
  _first (\c _first (\a
    let (\k1s \fopt Option.bind (\f
      Option.bind (\b
        let (List.filter (\at Option.match true (\_ false) (_res_var at)) f) $ \core
        Option.bind (\parts
          Option.bind (\rest
            Option.map (\rest2
              let (_gname (List.concat parts [b])) $ \gn
              △ (_replace c (_var gn) s) (△ (_sz gn) (List.concat k1s rest2)))
            (_remove (_sz b) rest))
          (_minus core e))
        (Option.sequence $ List.map
          (_atom4 Option.none Option.some (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none)) core))
      (List.foldr (\at \acc Option.alt (_res_var at) acc) Option.none f))
      fopt) $ \attempt
    # A machine that emits its successors outside the loop hands the chain on
    # without its head constructor, so the hypothesis is also tried against
    # the candidate under one synthesized stem; the missing node returns to
    # the spec as a literal 1, and the minted tree only gets smaller.
    Option.match (attempt [_one] (_fold a (_app △ c))) Option.some
      (attempt [] (_fold a c)))
    asms) (_subterms s)

# Case split: every tree is one of three shapes, every Snat one of two.
_stem = \w _app △ (_var w)
_shapes = \v let (_part Snat.zero v) $ \a let (_part Snat.one v) $ \b Bool.match
  [ △ △ []; △ (_stem a) [_one; _val a] ]
  [ △ △ [_one]
  ; △ (_stem a) [_one; _sz a]
  ; △ (_app (_stem a) (_var b)) [_one; _sz a; _sz b] ]

_cases = \recurse \s \v \rest _all
  (Pair.match $ \shape \atoms recurse (List.concat atoms rest) (Quoted.instantiate_eq v shape s))
_split = \recurse \e \s \v Option.match
  (\recurse Option.match (\_ false)
    (\rest \recurse _cases recurse s v rest $ _shapes v false) (_remove (_val v) e) recurse)
  (\rest \recurse _cases recurse s v rest $ _shapes v true)
  (_remove (_sz v) e) recurse

# The single-△-argument positions down a state's right application spine,
# each returned as the whole state with that occurrence replaced by [_var r]:
# the candidate seeds RGEN may generalise.
_rgen_sites = \r fix $ \self triage [] (\_ []) (\f \x
  List.concat (triage [△ f (_var r)] (\_ []) (\_ \_ []) x)
    (List.map (△ f) (self x)))

# ── REL: fold up to co-reduction with a paid difference ──────────────────────
# The record pair's step hands the loop itself in as its accumulator, so its
# states grow an argument list — self u₁ self u₂ self … v △ — that no state is
# ever an instance of, and the certifier climbs a tower it cannot close. Two
# rules end that, shared by both provers below.
#
#   REL(s, b, F): under every instantiation of their shared variables, s
#   evaluates to sum(F) more successors than b, wherever b's count is defined.
#
#   (S,Eh,v) ∈ Γ   σ = [v := w]   w strictly below v   REL(s, σS, E − σEh)
#   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── REL-FOLD
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E
#
# — the plain FOLD widened: the goal state need not be an instance of the
# hypothesis, it only has to cost a difference the spec can pay. REL itself is
# proved by co-reduction: normalize both sides, strip stems they emit in step,
# pay a stem only the left side emits with a 1 of the difference, close by
# syntactic identity once nothing is owed, case-split the variable both sides
# wait on (recording the goal PAIR as a hypothesis, reusable strictly below
# its split variable, other variables quantified as ever), and collapse the
# machine feeding itself forward with:
#
#   s = P·x·κC·T   REL(△(P·x·C·T), C·T, [|x|])   (the use obligation)
#   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── REL-USE
#   REL(s, b, F)   from   REL(C·T, △b, F − [|x|])
#
# P closed, x the variable s waits on, κC a seat whose head normalization is
# blocker-free at the closed value C ≠ △ (the reduction consulted no variable,
# so it reaches C under every instantiation — _seedish generalized), and T
# alternating (tree, seat) pairs whose seats reduce likewise to C, except the
# last, to △. The obligation says one △-wrap of the machine-at-x costs |x|
# over its own continuation at the same tail; the rewrite is then arithmetic:
# count(s) = |x| − 1 + count(C·T), so count(C·T) = (F − |x|) + count(△b).
# Obligations are stated for every valid tail and proven by induction on x
# alone — an obligation whose anchor (P and C, syntactically) matches an
# ancestor obligation's at a strictly smaller x is closed by that induction
# hypothesis outright, whatever its tail: on any concrete input the claims
# instantiate to statements about strict subtrees, so the descent grounds.
# An obligation reaching its own anchor at the same x fails instead. REL
# specs never carry a ⟨★⟩ or ⟨r⟩, so neither tail's semantics is ever read
# here, and no REL node can sit inside a phase for [_ends] to misread.
#
# USE's seat gate — closed, blocker-free, tailed — leaves out the machines
# that bank each deferred traversal in the continuation itself: their seat is
# an open, growing closure no _contish accepts, and the pair descent climbs a
# chain of bank layers no hypothesis is an instance of. USE∀ is USE with the
# seat abstracted in the obligation instead of normalized away:
#
#   s = P·x·seat   REL(△(P[x:=r̂]·x·ĉ), ĉ, [|x|])   ∀ x, ĉ, r̂
#   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── REL-USE∀
#   REL(s, b, F)   from   REL(seat, △b, F − [|x|])
#
# x the bare variable the state waits on, seat the single trailing argument
# (no tail), ĉ a fresh opaque seat variable and r̂ a fresh opaque variable
# standing for the prefix's carried copies of x. Nothing about the seat is
# assumed: the obligation is one statement over every seat and every copy,
# so the actual ones are plain ∀-instances — and inside the obligation's own
# proof the prefix is literally constant (the split substitutes shapes for x
# and its parts, never for r̂), so the fork case's grown bank layer is
# swallowed by the same family's induction hypothesis and no chain ever
# accretes. When both sides wait on the same x and both anchor, the two
# rewrites cancel the |x| − 1 and the difference passes untouched to the
# seat pair (USE∀²); a stem-wrapped anchor △(P·x·seat) costs |x| with no
# spare stem (USE∀ᵂ). Anchor keys canonicalize ĉ/r̂ identities by first
# appearance: closing by an ancestor whose key then matches is a bijective
# renaming of opaque, never-split, spec-free variables, an instance like any
# other. A seat carrying this very anchor's ĉ would make its own
# instantiation circular, and fails instead. These rules fire only under
# the normal-order judgment: eagerly a banked traversal is not a value, and
# the states these anchors describe never normalize.

_closedq = fix $ \self triage true (\_ false) (\f \x Bool.and (self f) (self x))
_cbudget = Snat.from_nat 2000
_contish = \x Option.bind (Pair.match $ \t \b Option.match
    (Bool.match Option.none (Option.some t) (_closedq t)) (\_ Option.none) b)
  (Quoted.head_normalize _cbudget x)
# Replace every argument down a state's spine that reduces blocker-free to a
# closed value by that value: a redex's parametric reduct, so the state's
# meaning is unchanged and spellings from different routes meet.
_seat_norm = fix $ \self triage △ (\n _var n)
  (\f \x _app (self f) (Option.match x id (_contish x)))
_stemq = triage Option.none (\_ Option.none)
  (\f \x triage (Option.some x) (\_ Option.none) (\_ \_ Option.none) f)
_spinel = \t (fix $ \self \t \acc triage (△ △ acc) (\n △ (_var n) acc)
  (\f \x self f (△ x acc)) t) t []
_unspine = List.foldl _app
_split_at_var = \x \args (fix $ \self \pre List.match Option.none (\hd \tl
  Bool.match (\u _at u self (△ hd pre) tl) (\u Option.some (△ (List.reverse pre) tl))
    (equal hd (_var x)) △)) [] args
# The trailing (tree, seat) pairs, seats normalized: C between, △ to close.
_tailn = \kv fix $ \self List.match Option.none (\v \tl List.match Option.none (\seat \tl2
  Option.bind (\cv List.match
      (triage (Option.some [v; △]) (\_ Option.none) (\_ \_ Option.none) cv)
      (\h2 \t2 Bool.match Option.none (Option.map (\r △ v (△ kv r)) (self tl2)) (equal cv kv))
      tl2)
    (_contish seat)) tl)
_usemark = [Snat.from_nat 10; Snat.from_nat 10]
# The anchor: △(P·x·C·T) and C·T as complete states, and the anchor key P·◇·C.
_use_pack = \hd \pre \x \c \tn Option.some (△
  (_app △ (_unspine hd (List.concat pre (△ (_var x) (△ c tn)))))
  (△ (_unspine c tn) (_unspine hd (List.concat pre [_var _usemark; c]))))
_rel_use_scan = \s \x Pair.let (_spinel s) $ \hd \args
  Bool.match Option.none
    (Option.bind (Pair.match $ \pre \rest
      Bool.match Option.none
        (List.match Option.none (\seat \tl
          Option.bind (\c
            Bool.match Option.none
              (Option.bind (\tn _use_pack hd pre x c tn) (_tailn c tl))
              (triage false (\_ true) (\_ \_ true) c))
            (_contish seat)) rest)
        (List.all _closedq pre))
      (_split_at_var x args))
    (triage true (\_ false) (\_ \_ false) hd)
# REL proof nodes, a small language of their own: [△ tag payload] with
#   0 SAME   1 FOLD (a pair hypothesis)   2 CASE (△ v kids)
#   3 USE (△ x (△ obligation continuation))   4 IH (an obligation closed by
#   the anchor induction)   5 USEP and 6 USEPW (△ x (△ obligation
#   continuation), the seat-polymorphic use, plain and stem-wrapped)
#   7 USEP2 (△ x (△ obligationL (△ obligationR continuation)), both sides
#   anchored at the shared x)
_rpf = \tag \payload △ tag payload
# One co-normalization round: both sides to value and blocker, stems aligned.
# Answers [△ state (△ blocker (△ state2 (△ blocker2 F)))], none on a budget.
_rstrips = Snat.from_nat 40
_rel_norm2 = \nfx fix $ \self \sfu \s \b \df
  Snat.match Option.none (\sfu
  Option.bind (Pair.match $ \sv \sb
  Option.bind (Pair.match $ \bv \bb
    Option.match
      (\u2 Option.some (△ sv (△ sb (△ bv (△ bb df)))))
      (\sx \u2 Option.match
        (\u3 Option.match (\u4 Option.some (△ sv (△ sb (△ bv (△ bb df)))))
          (\df2 \u4 _at u4 self sfu sx b df2) (_remove _one df) u3)
        (\bx \u3 _at u3 self sfu sx bx df)
        (_stemq bv) u2)
      (_stemq sv) △)
    (nfx b))
  (nfx s)) sfu
_rel_fold_try = \rasms \sn \bn \df _first (\h Pair.let h $ \hs \r Pair.let r $ \hb \r2
  Pair.let r2 $ \hf \v
  Option.bind (\s1 Option.bind (\s2
      Option.bind (\w Bool.match Option.none
        (Option.bind (\ren Bool.match Option.none (Option.some △) (_spec_eq ren df))
          (Option.sequence $ List.map (_rename s2) hf))
        (_below v w))
      (_image s2 v))
    (_match hb bn s1))
  (_match hs sn [])) rasms
_relsize = 6000
_reldepth = Snat.from_nat 5
_relwork = Snat.from_nat 400
# USE, always answering [△ fuel2 result] so what a failed attempt spent is
# spent for the split that follows it too.
_rel_try_use = \selfr \fuel \sn \bn \sb \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Option.match (\u △ fuel Option.none) (\x \u
    Option.match (\u2 △ fuel Option.none) (\df2 \u2
      Option.match (\u3 △ fuel Option.none) (\info \u3
        Pair.let info $ \wrapped \r Pair.let r $ \cont \pk
        (Bool.match
          (\u4 Bool.match
            (\u5 # prove the obligation, this anchor now in progress
              Pair.let (_at u5 selfr fuel wrapped cont [_sz x] [] (△ (△ pk x) obls) _reldepth) $
                \fuel2 \oblopt
              Option.match (\u6 △ fuel2 Option.none)
                (\obl \u6
                  Pair.let (_at u6 selfr fuel2 cont (_app △ bn) df2 rasms obls depth) $ \fuel3 \copt
                  △ fuel3 (Option.map (\cpf _rpf (Snat.from_nat 3) (△ x (△ obl cpf))) copt))
                oblopt △)
            (\u5 △ fuel Option.none)   # the anchor is this very obligation
            (List.any (equal (△ pk x)) obls) u4)
          (\u4 # closed by the anchor induction hypothesis
            Pair.let (_at u4 selfr fuel cont (_app △ bn) df2 rasms obls depth) $ \fuel3 \copt
            △ fuel3 (Option.map (\cpf _rpf (Snat.from_nat 3) (△ x (△ (_rpf (Snat.from_nat 4) △) cpf))) copt))
          (List.any (Pair.match $ \pk2 \x2 Bool.and (equal pk2 pk) (_extends x2 x)) obls) △))
        (_rel_use_scan sn x) u2)
      (_remove (_sz x) df) u)
    sb △
_kindq = List.match false (\h \tl Bool.or (equal h (Snat.from_nat 11)) (equal h (Snat.from_nat 12)))
# The split: the variable the left side waits on when the difference owes its
# size, else the variable both sides wait on, the difference untouched — case
# exhaustion needs no atom. The goal pair enters the hypotheses either way.
_rel_split = \selfr \nfx \fuel \sn \bn \sb \bb \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Snat.match (\_ △ fuel Option.none) (\d \_
  Option.match (\u △ fuel Option.none) (\v \u
    let (△ sn (△ bn (△ df v))) $ \hyp
    let (_remove (_sz v) df) $ \restF
    Pair.let ((fix $ \go \fuel \sh List.match (\_ △ fuel (Option.some []))
        (\hd \tl \_ Pair.let (Pair.let hd $ \shape \atoms
            _at shape selfr fuel
              (Quoted.instantiate_eq v shape sn) (Quoted.instantiate_eq v shape bn)
              (Option.match df (\rf List.concat atoms rf) restF)
              (△ hyp rasms) obls d) $ \fuel2 \sub
          Option.match (\u3 △ fuel2 Option.none)
            (\pf \u3 Pair.let (_at u3 go fuel2 tl) $ \fuel3 \rest
              △ fuel3 (Option.map (△ pf) rest))
            sub △)
        sh △) fuel (_shapes v true)) $ \fuel4 \kids
    △ fuel4 (Option.map (\ks _rpf Snat.two (△ v ks)) kids))
    (Option.bind (\x Option.match
        (Option.bind (\y Bool.match Option.none
            (Bool.match (Option.some x) Option.none (_kindq x))
            (equal x y)) bb)
        (\_ Option.some x)
        (_remove (_sz x) df))
      sb) △) depth △

# USE∀: the anchor P·x·seat, its obligation stated over an opaque seat ĉ and
# an opaque r̂ for the prefix's carried copies of x. The key canonicalizes
# ĉ/r̂ identities by first appearance so the family's statement is one term
# at every level.
_canon = \t0 Pair.fst $ (fix $ \self \t \env triage
    (△ △ env)
    (\n Bool.match (△ (_var n) env)
      ((fix $ \go \i \e List.match
          (△ (_var [Snat.from_nat 13; i]) (List.concat env [n]))
          (\h \tl Bool.match (go (Snat.succ i) tl) (△ (_var [Snat.from_nat 13; i]) env) (equal h n))
          e) Snat.zero env)
      (_kindq n))
    (\f \a Pair.let (self f env) $ \f2 \env2 Pair.let (self a env2) $ \a2 \env3 △ (_app f2 a2) env3)
    t) t0 []
# Answers [△ seat (△ wrapped (△ ĉ key))]: the actual seat for the rewrite,
# the obligation's sides, and the anchor key.
_rel_usep_scan = \s \x Pair.let (_spinel s) $ \hd \args
  (Bool.match (\u Option.none)
    (\u List.match (\u2 Option.none) (\seat \rev \u2
      List.match (\u3 Option.none) (\xv \prer \u3
        Bool.match (\u4 Option.none) (\u4
          List.match (\u5 Option.none) (\ph \pt \u5
            let (List.map (Quoted.instantiate_eq x (_var (△ (Snat.from_nat 12) x))) (List.reverse prer)) $ \pre
            let (_var (△ (Snat.from_nat 11) x)) $ \chat
            Option.some (△ seat (△
              (_app △ (_unspine hd (List.concat pre [_var x; chat])))
              (△ chat
                 (_canon (_unspine hd (List.concat pre [_var _usemark])))))))
            prer u4)
          (equal xv (_var x)) u3)
        rev u2)
      (List.reverse args) u)
    (triage true (\_ false) (\_ \_ false) hd)) △
_containsv = \n fix $ \self triage false (\m equal m n) (\f \a Bool.or (self f) (self a))
# Spawn or close a USE∀ obligation: by the family's induction hypothesis at a
# strictly smaller x, else proven fresh with this anchor in progress; a cycle
# at the same x, or a seat carrying this anchor's own ĉ (its instantiation
# would be circular), fails.
# A legitimate obligation closes in a handful of goals; a doomed one must
# fail cheaply. The sub-proof runs on its own small budget, and the caller
# is charged that budget flat.
_oblwork = Snat.from_nat 60
_charge = fix $ \self \n \fuel Snat.match (Option.some fuel) (\n2
  Snat.match Option.none (\f2 self n2 f2) fuel) n
_rel_oblp = \selfr \fuel \pack \x \obls
  Pair.let pack $ \seat \r1 Pair.let r1 $ \wrapped \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \chat \pk
  Bool.match
    (\u Bool.match
      (\u2 Option.match (\u3 △ fuel Option.none) (\fuel2 \u3
        Pair.let (_at u3 selfr _oblwork wrapped chat [_sz x] [] (△ (△ pk x) obls) _reldepth) $
          \spent \oblopt △ fuel2 oblopt)
        (_charge _oblwork fuel) u2)
      (\u2 △ fuel Option.none)
      (Bool.or (List.any (equal (△ pk x)) obls)
        (_containsv (△ (Snat.from_nat 11) x) seat)) u)
    (\u △ fuel (Option.some (_rpf (Snat.from_nat 4) △)))
    (List.any (Pair.match $ \pk2 \x2 Bool.and (equal pk2 pk) (_extends x2 x)) obls) △
# USE∀², both sides anchored at the shared blocked variable: the |x| − 1
# payments cancel and the difference passes untouched to the seat pair.
_rel_try_usep2 = \selfr \lz \fuel \sn \bn \sb \bb \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Bool.match (\u △ fuel Option.none) (\u
    Option.match (\u2 △ fuel Option.none) (\x \u2
      Option.match (\u3 △ fuel Option.none) (\x2 \u3
        Bool.match (\u4 △ fuel Option.none) (\u4
          Option.match (\u5 △ fuel Option.none) (\pl \u5
            Option.match (\u6 △ fuel Option.none) (\pr \u6
              Pair.let (_at u6 _rel_oblp selfr fuel pl x obls) $ \fuel2 \olopt
              Option.match (\u7 △ fuel2 Option.none) (\ol \u7
                Pair.let (_at u7 _rel_oblp selfr fuel2 pr x obls) $ \fuel3 \oropt
                Option.match (\u8 △ fuel3 Option.none) (\og \u8
                  Pair.let pl $ \seatl \rl
                  Pair.let pr $ \seatr \rr
                  Pair.let (_at u8 selfr fuel3 seatl seatr df rasms obls depth) $ \fuel4 \copt
                  △ fuel4 (Option.map (\c _rpf (Snat.from_nat 7) (△ x (△ ol (△ og c)))) copt))
                  oropt △)
                olopt △)
              (_rel_usep_scan bn x) △)
            (_rel_usep_scan sn x) △)
          (equal x x2) u3)
        bb △)
      sb △)
    lz △
# USE∀ plain: pay |x|, the spare stem landing on b as in USE.
_rel_try_usep = \selfr \lz \fuel \sn \bn \sb \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Bool.match (\u △ fuel Option.none) (\u
    Option.match (\u2 △ fuel Option.none) (\x \u2
      Option.match (\u3 △ fuel Option.none) (\df2 \u3
        Option.match (\u4 △ fuel Option.none) (\pl \u4
          Pair.let (_at u4 _rel_oblp selfr fuel pl x obls) $ \fuel2 \oblopt
          Option.match (\u5 △ fuel2 Option.none) (\obl \u5
            Pair.let pl $ \seat \rl
            Pair.let (_at u5 selfr fuel2 seat (_app △ bn) df2 rasms obls depth) $ \fuel3 \copt
            △ fuel3 (Option.map (\c _rpf (Snat.from_nat 5) (△ x (△ obl c))) copt))
            oblopt △)
          (_rel_usep_scan sn x) △)
        (_remove (_sz x) df) △)
      sb △)
    lz △
# USE∀ wrapped: s = △(P·x·seat) costs |x| with no spare stem — the stem the
# strip loop could not pay is the obligation's own wrapper.
_rel_try_usepw = \selfr \nfx \lz \fuel \sn \bn \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Bool.match (\u △ fuel Option.none) (\u
    Option.match (\u2 △ fuel Option.none) (\inner \u2
      Option.match (\u3 △ fuel Option.none) (\nr \u3
        Pair.let nr $ \iv \ibo
        Option.match (\u4 △ fuel Option.none) (\x \u4
          Option.match (\u5 △ fuel Option.none) (\df2 \u5
            Option.match (\u6 △ fuel Option.none) (\pl \u6
              Pair.let (_at u6 _rel_oblp selfr fuel pl x obls) $ \fuel2 \oblopt
              Option.match (\u7 △ fuel2 Option.none) (\obl \u7
                Pair.let pl $ \seat \rl
                Pair.let (_at u7 selfr fuel2 seat bn df2 rasms obls depth) $ \fuel3 \copt
                △ fuel3 (Option.map (\c _rpf (Snat.from_nat 6) (△ x (△ obl c))) copt))
                oblopt △)
              (_rel_usep_scan iv x) △)
            (_remove (_sz x) df) △)
          ibo △)
        (nfx inner) △)
      (_stemq sn) △)
    lz △
_rel_use_or_split = \selfr \nfx \lz \fuel \sn \bn \sb \bb \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Pair.let (_rel_try_use selfr fuel sn bn sb df rasms obls depth) $ \fuel2 \useopt
  Option.match (\u
    Pair.let (_at u _rel_try_usep2 selfr lz fuel2 sn bn sb bb df rasms obls depth) $ \fuel3 \p2opt
    Option.match (\u2
      Pair.let (_at u2 _rel_try_usep selfr lz fuel3 sn bn sb df rasms obls depth) $ \fuel4 \p1opt
      Option.match (\u3
        Pair.let (_at u3 _rel_try_usepw selfr nfx lz fuel4 sn bn df rasms obls depth) $ \fuel5 \pwopt
        Option.match (\u4 _at u4 _rel_split selfr nfx fuel5 sn bn sb bb df rasms obls depth)
          (\pf \u4 △ fuel5 (Option.some pf))
          pwopt △)
        (\pf \u3 △ fuel4 (Option.some pf))
        p1opt △)
      (\pf \u2 △ fuel3 (Option.some pf))
      p2opt △)
    (\pf \u △ fuel2 (Option.some pf))
    useopt △
# _rel nfx fuel q b F rasms obls depth — always [△ fuel2 result], the spent
# fuel returned through failures too, so the work one attempt may do is
# bounded whether or not its branches close.
# When the full-form budget fails and the head normalization answers a stem
# value, the blocker is inside: surface it, as the full form would have, but
# only where it decides anything — a goal whose right side is a bare variable,
# an obligation's ĉ, whose induction needs the split on x. A few levels
# suffice (the wrapped anchors are one stem deep) and the descent stops at
# the first blocker; everywhere else the old fail-fast behavior stands.
_stem_blocker = fix $ \self \d \t Snat.match Option.none (\d2
  Option.match Option.none (\x
    Option.match Option.none (Pair.match $ \xv \xb
      Option.match (\u _at u self d2 xv) (\bk \u Option.some bk) xb △)
    (Quoted.head_normalize _cbudget x))
  (_stemq t)) d
_rel = \nfx \lz fix $ \selfr \fuel \q \b \df \rasms \obls \depth
  Snat.match (△ △ Option.none) (\fuel
  Option.match (\u △ fuel Option.none) (\nr \u
    Pair.let nr $ \sv \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \sb0 \r3 Pair.let r3 $ \bv \r4 Pair.let r4 $ \bb \df
    let (Option.match
      (\u5 Bool.match (\u6 Option.none)
        (\u6 triage Option.none (\n2 _stem_blocker (Snat.from_nat 4) sv) (\f2 \a2 Option.none) bv)
        lz u5)
      (\x2 \u5 Option.some x2) sb0 △) $ \sb
    (Bool.match (\u2 △ fuel Option.none) (\u2
      let (_seat_norm sv) $ \sn
      let (_seat_norm bv) $ \bn
      (Bool.match
        (\u3 Option.match
          (\u4 _at u4 _rel_use_or_split selfr nfx lz fuel sn bn sb bb df rasms obls depth)
          (\_ \u4 △ fuel (Option.some (_rpf Snat.one △)))
          (_rel_fold_try rasms sn bn df) u3)
        (\u3 △ fuel (Option.some (_rpf Snat.zero △)))
        (Bool.and (List.is_empty df) (equal sn bn)) △))
      (Nat.is_lte (size sv) _relsize) △))
    (_rel_norm2 nfx _rstrips q b df) △) fuel
# One hypothesis, one paid difference: σ sends the hypothesis's only variable
# — its split variable — to a tree variable the goal's spec owes, strictly
# below it, and REL pays the rest. Answers [△ w proof].
_only_var = \v fix $ \self triage true (\n equal n v) (\f \x Bool.and (self f) (self x))
_tree_atom = _atom4 Option.none Option.some (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none)
_rel_try1 = \nfx \lz \q \e \hst \spec \v
  (Bool.match (\u Option.none) (\u
    _at u _first (\at2 Option.match Option.none (\w
        (Bool.match (\u2 Option.none) (\u2
          Option.bind (\df
            Option.map (△ w) $ Pair.snd $
              _at df _rel nfx lz _relwork q (Quoted.instantiate_eq v (_var w) hst) df [] [] _reldepth)
            (Option.bind (\ren _minus ren e)
              (Option.sequence $ List.map (_rename [△ v (_var w)]) spec)))
          (_below v w)) △)
        (_tree_atom at2)) e)
    (Bool.and (Bool.not (_closedq hst)) (_only_var v hst))) △
_rel_stage_e = \nf \q \asms \e
  (Bool.match
    (\u Option.match false (\_ true) $ _at u _first (\a Pair.let a $ \hst \r
      Pair.let r $ \spec \v _at v _rel_try1 nf false q e hst spec v) asms)
    (\u false)
    (_has_res e)) △

# The prover. Every branch that can recurse is handed `self` only once it is
# taken: under eager reduction a recursive call fires as soon as its arguments
# are bound, whether or not its branch was selected, so an unguarded `self` here
# would unfold the whole search space rather than the path the proof takes.
_depth = Snat.from_nat 6
_prove = \nf fix $ \self \depth \g \asms \e \q
  Option.match (\_ false) (Pair.match $ \s \blocked \self       # NORMALIZE
    # SPLIT, held back until a branch below asks for it. The goal being split
    # is what enters `asms`, so it is available as a hypothesis from here down.
    let (\self Snat.match (\_ false) (\d \_ Option.match (\_ false)
          (\v \_ _split (self d g $ △ (△ s (△ e v)) asms) e s v) blocked self) depth self) $ \split
    # RGEN, when the split fails: a literal △ in argument position down the
    # state's application spine — the seed — is generalised to an opaque
    # residual and the goal retried, so that the hypothesis the next split
    # records ranges over every accumulator rather than the empty one.
    # Proving the goal under ⟨r⟩ proves it at r := △, and ⟨△⟩ is the plain
    # judgment.
    let (\self Bool.match
          (\u Bool.match (\u2 false)
             (\u2 let (_fresh g) $ \r
                Option.match false (\_ true) $
                _first (\s2 Bool.match Option.none (Option.some △)
                         (_at s2 self depth (Snat.succ g) asms (△ (_res r) e) s2))
                  (_rgen_sites r s))
             (Bool.not (_has_res e)) u)
          (\u true)
          (split self) △) $ \split2
    Bool.match                                                  # FOLD, else …
      (\self Option.match                                       # … GENERALIZE, else …
        (\self Option.match                                     # … GEN-TREE, else REL-FOLD, else read s off:
          (\self Bool.match
            (\self triage
              (\_ List.is_empty e)                              # a leaf is zero
              (\v \_ Bool.or (_spec_eq e [_val v]) (_spec_eq e [_res v]))  # a bare variable
              (\f \x \self triage
                (\self Option.match (\self split2 self)         # [△ x] is a successor: PEEL a 1
                  (\e2 \self self depth g asms e2 x) (_remove _one e) self)
                (\_ \self split2 self)                          # stuck under a variable
                (\ff \_ \self triage (\_ false) (\_ \self split2 self) (\_ \_ \self split2 self) ff self)
                f self)                                         # …a fork is not an Snat; else stuck
              s self)
            (\self true)
            (_at self _rel_stage_e nf q asms e) self)
          (\gen \self Pair.let gen $ \s2 \e2 self depth g asms e2 s2)
          (_at self _gen_tree asms e s) self)
        (\gen \self Pair.let gen $ \s2 \e2 self depth (Snat.succ g) asms e2 s2)
        (_generalize (_fresh g) asms e s) self)
      (\_ true)
      (List.any (\a Option.match false (_spec_eq e) $ _fold a s) asms)
      self)
  (nf q) self

# The two reduction orders, as the two normalizers the prover runs on. Both
# normalize all the way down and both answer [none] rather than not returning,
# so which one the prover is handed decides what a verdict means, not whether
# there is one. Where both return they return the same normal form — reduction
# is confluent — so running the lazy one over the eager one's result is not more
# reduction, only the blocker read off it.
_budget = Snat.from_nat 1000            # rule applications, eagerly
_head_budget = Snat.from_nat 40000      # head reductions, in normal order
_lazily = Quoted.normalize_lazy _head_budget
_eagerly = \q Option.bind _lazily $ Quoted.normalize_eager _budget q

_certify = \nf \p _prove nf _depth Snat.one [] [_sz _input] $ _app (Reflect.quote p) (_var _input)

# computes_size_eagerly p — [computes_size] and more: [p t] terminates in
# every reduction order. False means "not certifiable here" as before, and now
# covers running out of budget too, which is what makes this one total.
computes_size_eagerly = _certify _eagerly

# ── The lazy certifier ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is [computes_size]: the prover above, extended until the
# __wn programs admit certificates, and returning a proof tree that a second
# pass re-checks. The eager certificate keeps the prover above unchanged,
# because one extension below is sound in normal order only.
#
# The judgment is the same   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E   and the base rules carry over:
#
#   ───────────── ZERO           ────────────── VALUE
#   Γ ⊢ △ ⊨ ∅                   Γ ⊢ n ⊨ [n]
#
#   Γ ⊢ x ⊨ E                    Γ, (S,E,v) ⊢ S[v:=σᵢ] ⊨ Eᵢ   (every shape σᵢ)
#   ────────────────── PEEL      ─────────────────────────────────────── SPLIT
#   Γ ⊢ △x ⊨ E ⊎ [1]            Γ ⊢ S ⊨ E
#
#   (S,Eₕ,v) ∈ Γ   σS ≡ s   σv strictly below v   σEₕ = E
#   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── FOLD
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E
#
#   (S,Eₕ,v) ∈ Γ   σS ≡ c ≤ s   σEₕ ⊆ E   n fresh
#   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── GENERALIZE
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E   from   Γ ⊢ s[c:=n] ⊨ (E − σEₕ) ⊎ [n]
#
# Seven additions. Three are this prover's own, each forced by a measured
# obstruction of the __wn programs and none needed by the eager ones:
#
# SPEC-SPLIT. A lazy program emits successors before consulting its input, so
# reduction is not blocked on any variable and the SPLIT above never fires.
# Every tree has at least one node, so a |v| owed in the spec licenses the
# same split without a blocker. Same shapes, same soundness.
#
# ABSTRACT. These machines carry copies of the input that lag one constructor
# behind the live occurrence, so no state is ever an instance of a hypothesis
# and FOLD never closes. Anti-unification against a hypothesis a fold could
# use finds the lag junk, and each junk position is replaced by a fresh
# opaque variable:
#
#   Γ ⊢ s[p₁:=J₁, …, pₖ:=Jₖ] ⊨ E      (Jᵢ fresh, small junk only)
#   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── ABSTRACT
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E
#
# Sound because an opaque variable stands for an arbitrary tree and nothing
# can ever case on the Jᵢ — splitting needs the variable in the spec, and
# they are not. Instantiating them back recovers the goal — for junk that
# diverges under eager evaluation too, which is why this rule is what makes
# the certificate normal-order only, and why the eager prover keeps none of
# this.
#
# CUT and ⟨★⟩. Splitting a fork rewrites |v| to [1,|a|,|b|], so left-nested
# forks grow the spec without bound and no finite family of hypotheses closes
# the induction. The spec gains a tail atom ⟨★⟩, "and then whatever the
# continuation owes", at most one per spec:
#
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E ⊎ [⟨★⟩]     Γ ⊢ es ⊨ F   (every state es the phase ends in)
#   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── CUT
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ E ⊎ F
#
#   ────────────────── ★ (records s as an end state)
#   Γ ⊢ s ⊨ [⟨★⟩]
#
# The phase proof shows s emits E and then reaches one of finitely many end
# states; each end state owes what was cut away; composition gives E ⊎ F.
# FOLD treats ⟨★⟩ as an atom present on both sides or neither — and a fold
# whose hypothesis was recorded under a different tail than the goal's
# borrows that hypothesis's end states for another continuation. That is
# sound exactly when those ends also satisfy the borrowing cut's spec, which
# is what [_validate] re-checks across the finished proof before a verdict.
#
# The last four additions are the eager prover's own, shared: RGEN and
# GEN-TREE, ported — a chain machine recurses on a rebuilt tree no
# structural FOLD closes, and the weak record pair drives exactly the eager
# record's chain step, the 95's, tree for tree. Both rules survive the
# change of judgment as they stand, ⟨r⟩ meaning normal-order evaluation to
# r under sum(E) successors. What the port adds is spelled at their
# definitions: a seed is whatever head-normalizes to △ without consulting a
# variable, the instance match runs on both sides' standalone normal forms,
# and each rule keeps to res-owing, star-free specs — so neither tail's
# semantics ever reads the other's, and no RGEN or GEN-TREE node can sit
# inside a phase for [_ends] to misread. And REL-FOLD with REL-USE, one
# definition serving both provers on their own normalizers, gated star- and
# res-free the same way: what they are and why they are sound is at their
# definitions, and they are what certifies the record pair — the 78 here,
# where RGEN's opaque residual blocks the accumulator-reading step, and the
# 90 under both judgments.

# The spec gains a fourth atom: [△ (△ △) k] is ⟨★k⟩, "then whatever the
# continuation k owes". At most one per spec. RGEN further down adds a
# fifth, [△ (△ △ △) r] — the eager certifier's ⟨r⟩ read under the
# normal-order judgment: a state owing E ⊎ [⟨r⟩] evaluates to r under
# sum(E) successors. Also at most one per spec, and never beside a ⟨★⟩:
# RGEN refuses starred goals and CUT refuses residualed ones, so the two
# tails never meet and each keeps its one semantics.
_starx = \k △ (△ △) k
_resx = \r △ (△ △ △) r
_atomx = \o1 \osz \oval \ostar \ores triage o1 osz (\c \v triage (oval v) (\_ ostar v) (\_ \_ ores v) c)
_is_star = _atomx false (\_ false) (\_ false) (\_ true) (\_ false)
_is_res = _atomx false (\_ false) (\_ false) (\_ false) (\_ true)
_star_name = _atomx Option.none (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none) (\k Option.some k) (\_ Option.none)
_core = List.filter (\a Bool.not (_is_star a))
_stars = List.filter _is_star
_has_resx = List.any _is_res
_atom_var = _atomx Option.none Option.some Option.some Option.none Option.none

# Fresh names carry the proof path, so every star and hypothesis id minted
# anywhere in the tree is globally distinct; the leading Snat says what kind
# of name it is, and no tree variable starts above one (parts prepend 0 or 1).
_n3 = Snat.succ Snat.two
_n4 = Snat.succ _n3
_n5 = Snat.succ _n4
_n6 = Snat.succ _n5
_n7 = Snat.succ _n6
_n8 = Snat.succ _n7
_n9 = Snat.succ _n8
_n10 = Snat.succ _n9
_n11 = Snat.succ _n10
_genname = \p △ Snat.two p
_jname = \i \p △ _n3 (△ i p)
_starname = \p △ _n4 p
_resname = \p △ _n5 p

# Hypotheses: [△ state (△ spec (△ split_variable id))].
# [_foldx] matches a hypothesis against a state: the split variable must land
# strictly below itself — [_below], so a variable GEN-TREE minted from
# disjoint proper parts counts — the renamed size atoms must be exactly the
# goal's, and a tail is bridged whenever both sides have one — a bridge
# across two different tails borrows the hypothesis's end states for
# another cut's continuation, so it is recorded and re-checked by
# [_validate] afterwards. A ⟨r⟩ atom renames like a size atom: the residual
# must land on a variable.
_renamex = \s _atomx (Option.some _one) (\v Option.map _sz $ _image s v)
  (\v Option.map _val $ _image s v) (\_ Option.none) (\v Option.map _resx $ _image s v)
_foldx = \a \t Pair.let a $ \state \r Pair.let r $ \spec \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \v \hid
  Option.bind (\s Option.bind
    (\w Bool.match Option.none
      (Option.map (\renamed △ renamed (△ (List.foldr (\at \acc Option.alt (_star_name at) acc) Option.none spec) (△ s hid)))
        (Option.sequence $ List.map (_renamex s) (_core spec)))
      (_below v w))
    (_image s v))
    (_match state t [])

# Proof nodes: [△ tag payload], tag an Snat.
#   0 zero   1 value   2 peel   3 split   4 fold   5 generalize
#   6 abstract   7 cut   8 end-of-phase   9 rgen   10 gen-tree   11 rel-fold
_pf = \tag \payload △ tag payload
# Handlers take the payload; picking one costs only the tag walk.
_pf_case = \p \z \va \pe \sp \fo \ge \ab \cu \st \rg \gt \rl Pair.let p $ \tag \pay
  (Snat.match z (\t1 Snat.match va (\t2 Snat.match pe
  (\t3 Snat.match sp (\t4 Snat.match fo (\t5 Snat.match ge
  (\t6 Snat.match ab (\t7 Snat.match cu (\t8 Snat.match st
  (\t9 Snat.match rg (\t10 Snat.match gt (\_ rl) t10) t9) t8) t7) t6) t5) t4) t3) t2) t1) tag) pay

# The states a phase ends in: every tag-8 leaf naming this tail. An abstract
# (or generalize) node proved its subtree for fresh variables standing for
# concrete subterms, so its ends cover the original by instantiation:
# substitute back on the way out, or the continuation loses what the phase
# abstracted away.
_ends = \star fix $ \self \p _pf_case p
  (\_ [])
  (\_ [])
  self
  (Pair.match $ \_ \kids List.concat_list (List.map self kids))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \nc \sub Pair.let nc $ \n \c List.map (Quoted.instantiate_eq n c) (self sub))
  (Pair.match $ \subst \sub List.map (Quoted.apply_record subst) (self sub))
  (Pair.match $ \_ Pair.match $ \phase \obls List.concat (self phase) (List.concat_list $ List.map self obls))
  (Pair.match $ \st \state Bool.match [] [state] (equal st star))
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (\_ [])

# ── ABSTRACT: induction strengthening ────────────────────────────────────────
# Walk hypothesis state and goal state in parallel, collecting every variable
# capture and every structural mismatch with its path (a list: true = into the
# function, false = into the argument).
_collect = fix $ \self \p \t \path \acc triage
  (triage acc (\_ Pair.map_snd (△ (△ path t)) acc) (\_ \_ Pair.map_snd (△ (△ path t)) acc) t)
  (\n Pair.map_fst (△ (△ n (△ path t))) acc)
  (\pf \px triage
    (Pair.map_snd (△ (△ path t)) acc)
    (\_ Pair.map_snd (△ (△ path t)) acc)
    (\tf \tx self px tx (△ false path) $ self pf tf (△ true path) acc)
    t)
  p

_replace_at = fix $ \self \path \sub \t List.match sub
  (\hd \tl triage △ (\a △ a)
    (\f \x (Bool.match (\_ △ f (self tl sub x)) (\_ △ (self tl sub f) x) hd) △) t)
  path

# The lag junk of one state against a hypothesis a fold could use: positions
# where the split variable captured anything but its strictly-smaller image.
# A capture that is itself a strictly-smaller variable is another live
# position, never junk. Junk is small (the measured lag is 2-7 nodes); a
# large mismatch is live structure, and abstracting it only wastes the search.
# Size in nodes of the tree a quoted term stands for, not of its encoding: a
# variable is one node however long its name, an application spine one node
# plus its arguments'. The junk cap is calibrated in this metric — the lag a
# machine carries is two to seven nodes of value, whatever that costs to spell.
_psize = fix $ \self triage 1 (\_ 1) (\f \x Nat.add (self f) (self x))
_small = \t Nat.is_lte (_psize t) 12
_compat = \e \spec Bool.and
  (equal (List.length (_core spec)) (List.length (_core e)))
  (equal (List.is_empty (_stars spec)) (List.is_empty (_stars e)))
_is_below_var = \w \t triage false (\u _extends w u) (\_ \_ false) t
_worth = \t triage true (\_ false) (\_ \_ true) t
_junk_of = \w \caps \hards
  let (List.map Pair.snd (List.filter (Pair.match $ \n \_ equal n w) caps)) $ \wcaps
  Option.bind (\_
    let (List.filter (Pair.match $ \_ _worth) (List.concat
          (List.filter (Pair.match $ \_ \t Bool.not (_is_below_var w t)) wcaps) hards)) $ \junk
    (Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.some junk) (Bool.and
      (Bool.and (Bool.not (List.is_empty junk)) (Nat.is_lte (List.length junk) 4))
      (List.all (Pair.match $ \_ _small) junk)) △))
    (_first (Pair.match $ \_ \t Bool.match Option.none (Option.some t) (_is_below_var w t)) wcaps)

# Replace each distinct junk subterm with one fresh opaque variable. Nothing
# can ever case on those variables — splitting needs the variable in the spec
# — so proving the strengthened state proves the original at any
# instantiation, divergent junk included. Sound in normal order only, which is
# the certificate this prover issues.
_abstractx = \path \asms \e \s
  _first (\a Pair.let a $ \state \r Pair.let r $ \spec \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \v \_
    (Bool.match (\u2 Option.none) (\u2
      Pair.let (_at u2 _collect state s [] (△ [] [])) $ \caps \hards
      Option.bind (\junk
        Pair.let ((fix $ \self List.match (\_ △ [] [])
              (\hd \tl \i Pair.let hd $ \pth \t
                Pair.let (self tl (Snat.succ i)) $ \names \subst
                Option.match
                  (△ (△ (△ t (_jname i path)) names) (△ (△ (_jname i path) t) subst))
                  (\_ △ names subst)
                  (List.lookup t names))) junk Snat.zero) $ \names \subst
        let (List.foldr (Pair.match $ \pth \t \acc Option.match acc
              (\nm _replace_at (List.reverse pth) (_var nm) acc) (List.lookup t names)) s junk) $ \s2
        (Bool.match (\_ Option.some (△ s2 subst)) (\_ Option.none) (equal s2 s) △))
        (_junk_of v caps hards))
      (_compat e spec) △))
    asms

# ── CUT: the tail ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which variable is the machine working on now? Leaf every other spec variable
# and count emissions until it blocks on v: the subject in hand blocks
# earliest. A bounded probe, for candidate order only.
_pbudget = Snat.from_nat 2000
_nf_probe = \q (Option.match
  (\u _at u Quoted.head_normalize _pbudget q)
  (\r \_ Option.some r)
  (Quoted.normalize_lazy _pbudget q)) △
_rank = \e \s \v
  let (List.foldr (\a \q Option.match q
        (\w Bool.match (Quoted.instantiate_eq w △ q) q (equal w v))
        (_atom_var a)) s (_core e)) $ \q0
  (fix $ \self \fuel \n \q Snat.match (Snat.from_nat 600) (\fuel2
    Option.match
      (\u2 Snat.from_nat 900)
      (Pair.match $ \r \bopt \u2
        (Bool.match
          (\u3 Snat.from_nat 900)
          (\u3 (triage
            (\u4 (triage (\u5 Snat.from_nat 700) (\w2 \u5 Snat.from_nat 700) (\rf \rx \u5
                (triage (\u6 _at u6 self fuel2 (Snat.succ n) rx)
                  (\_ \u6 Snat.from_nat 700) (\_ \_ \u6 Snat.from_nat 700) rf) u5)
              r) u4)
            (\w \u4 Bool.match (Snat.from_nat 800) n (equal w v))
            (\_ \_ \u4 Snat.from_nat 800)
            bopt) u3)
          (Nat.is_lte (size r) 4000)) u2)
      (_at fuel2 _nf_probe q) fuel2) fuel) (Snat.from_nat 25) Snat.zero q0
_insert_ranked = \x fix $ \self List.match [x]
  (\hd \tl (Bool.match (\tl2 △ hd (self tl2)) (\tl2 △ x (△ hd tl2))
    (Snat.is_lt (Pair.fst x) (Pair.fst hd))) tl)
_sort_ranked = fix $ \self List.match [] (\hd \tl _insert_ranked hd (self tl))

# Partition the spec around v: its own atoms (and the 1s) stay in the phase,
# the rest is what the phase's end states will owe.

# Partition the spec around v: the 1s and v's own atoms stay in the phase,
# everything else — the tail included — is what the phase's ends will owe.
_keeps = \v \a Option.match (equal a _one)
  (\w Bool.or (equal w v) (_extends v w)) (_atom_var a)
_partition = \v \e △ (List.filter (_keeps v) e) (List.filter (\a Bool.not (_keeps v a)) e)

_dedupe = fix $ \self List.match []
  (\hd \tl (Bool.match (\tl2 △ hd (self tl2)) (\tl2 self tl2) (List.any (equal hd) tl)) tl)
_dedupe_first = fix $ \self \seen List.match []
  (\hd \tl (Bool.match (\tl2 △ hd (_at tl2 self (△ hd seen) tl2)) (\tl2 _at tl2 self seen tl2)
    (List.any (equal hd) seen)) tl)

# Map a fallible prover over a list with an index, first failure aborting; the
# tail travels through the branch as its argument, so a later element is only
# attempted once the earlier ones succeed.
_mapxi = \f fix $ \self \i List.match (Option.some [])
  (\hd \tl Option.match (\tl2 Option.none)
    (\r \tl2 Option.map (△ r) (_at tl2 self (Snat.succ i) tl2)) (f i hd) tl)

# GENERALIZE, against star-free hypothesis instances only.
_generalizex = \g \asms \e \s
  _first (\c _first (\a Option.bind (Pair.match $ \core \r2
    (triage
      (\_ Option.map (\rest △ (_at rest _replace c (_var g) s) (△ (△ (_val g) rest) c)) (_minus core e))
      (\_ \_ Option.none)
      (\_ \_ \_ Option.none)
      (Pair.fst r2)) △) $ _foldx a c) asms) (_subterms s)

# Try alternatives in order. Each element is a function of a throwaway
# argument, applied only when its turn comes, and the recursion into the tail
# receives that argument too — self and tl alone would form an application
# eager reduction runs while the branch is still being built.
_try = fix $ \self \u List.match Option.none (\hd \tl
  (triage (\u2 self u2 tl) (\x \_ Option.some x) (\_ \_ \_ Option.none) (hd u)) △)

# The prover. Each rule lives in its own top-level definition; [_at] and the
# argument-threading inside each rule keep every recursive call out of reach
# until the branch that makes it is the one taken.
_stg_fold = \gstar \asms \e \s _first (\a Option.bind (Pair.match $ \core \r2
    Pair.let r2 $ \staropt \r3 Pair.let r3 $ \sigma \hid
    (Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_ (Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.some $ _pf _n4 $
        Option.match Option.none (\hs Option.match Option.none (\gs
            (Bool.match (\_ Option.some (△ hs (△ gs (△ sigma hid)))) (\_ Option.none) (equal hs gs) △))
            gstar) staropt)
      (_spec_eq (_core e) core) △))
    (equal (Option.match false (\_ true) staropt) (Option.match false (\_ true) gstar)) △))
  (_foldx a s)) asms
_stg_star = \e \s List.match Option.none (\hd \tl (Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_
    Option.match Option.none (\st Option.some (_pf _n8 (△ st s))) (_star_name hd))
    (Bool.and (_is_star hd) (List.is_empty tl)) △)) e
_stg_cut_cand = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s \rv Pair.let rv $ \_ \v
  Pair.let (_partition v e) $ \keep \cut
  (Bool.match (\u2 Option.none) (\u2
    let (△ _n5 (△ v path)) $ \cpath
    let (_starname cpath) $ \st
    Option.match
      (\u3 Option.none)
      (\phase \u3
        Option.match (\u4 Option.none)
          (\obls \u4 Option.some $ _pf _n7 $ △ (△ st (△ cut asms)) (△ phase obls))
          (_at phase _mapxi (\i \es _at es selfp es depth (△ i (△ _n8 cpath)) true asms cut)
            Snat.zero (_dedupe (_ends st phase)))
          u3)
      (_at u2 selfp s depth (△ _n7 cpath) true asms (List.concat keep [_starx st]))
      u2)
    (Bool.and (Bool.not (List.is_empty (_core cut))) (Bool.not (List.is_empty (_core keep)))))
  △
_stg_cut = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s \blocked
  (Bool.match (\u2 Option.none) (\u2
    let (List.take 3 $ _dedupe_first []
          (List.concat (Option.match [] (\w [w]) blocked)
            (List.foldr (\a \acc Option.match acc (\w2 △ w2 acc) (_atom_var a)) [] (_core e)))) $ \cands
    _at u2 _first (_stg_cut_cand selfp depth path asms e s)
      (List.match [] (\c1 \tl (Bool.match
        (\tl2 _sort_ranked $ List.map (\v2 △ (_rank e s v2) v2) (△ c1 tl2))
        (\tl2 [△ Snat.zero c1])
        (List.is_empty tl)) tl) cands))
    (Bool.and (Bool.not (_has_resx e)) (Nat.is_lte 2 (List.length (_core e))))) △
_stg_abs = \selfp \depth \path \ca \asms \e \s
  (Bool.match (\u2 (Bool.match (\u3 Option.none) (\u3
    Option.match (\u4 Option.none) (\cand \u4
      Pair.let cand $ \s2 \subst
      Option.map (\sub _pf _n6 (△ subst sub))
        (_at u4 selfp s2 depth (△ _n6 path) false asms e))
      (_at u3 _abstractx path asms e s)
      u3) ca) u2)
    (\u2 Option.none)
    (Bool.or (List.is_empty asms) (_has_resx e))) △
_split_at = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s \v
  Snat.match Option.none (\d
    let (△ s (△ e (△ v path))) $ \hyp
    let (\rest \sh _mapxi (\i Pair.match $ \shape \atoms
          _at shape selfp (Quoted.instantiate_eq v shape s) d (△ i path) true (△ hyp asms)
            (List.concat atoms rest))
          Snat.zero sh) $ \go
    Option.map (\kids _pf _n3 (△ (△ v path) kids)) $
      (Option.match
        (\u2 Option.match (\u3 Option.none) (\rest \u3 _at u3 go rest (_shapes v false))
          (_remove (_val v) e) u2)
        (\rest \u2 _at u2 go rest (_shapes v true))
        (_remove (_sz v) e) △))
    depth
_stg_split = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s \blocked
  Option.match
    (\u2 _at u2 _first (\a Option.match (\u3 Option.none)
      (\v \u3 _at u3 _split_at selfp depth path asms e s v) (_atom_var a) a) e)
    (\v \u2 _at u2 _split_at selfp depth path asms e s v)
    blocked △

# RGEN, ported from the eager prover: when the split fails on a plain goal —
# no assumptions yet, no tail of either kind — an accumulator seed down the
# state's right application spine becomes an opaque residual r and the goal
# is retried owing ⟨r⟩, so that the hypothesis the next split records ranges
# over every accumulator. Proving the goal under ⟨r⟩ proves it at r := △,
# and ⟨△⟩ is the plain judgment, a stack over a leaf being an Snat. One lazy
# widening: a whnf state still spells its k seat [const △ t] where the eager
# states have long reduced it, so a seed is any argument whose head normal
# form is △ with no blocker — a reduction that inspected no variable, so it
# reaches △ under every instantiation and r := △ still recovers the goal.
_sbudget = Snat.from_nat 100
_seedish = \x Option.match false (Pair.match $ \t \b
    Option.match (triage true (\_ false) (\_ \_ false) t) (\_ false) b)
  (Quoted.head_normalize _sbudget x)
_rgen_sitesx = \r fix $ \self triage [] (\_ []) (\f \x
  List.concat (Bool.match [] [△ f (_var r)] (_seedish x))
    (List.map (△ f) (self x)))
_stg_split2 = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s \blocked
  Option.match
    (\u2 (Bool.match (\u3 Option.none) (\u3
        let (_resname path) $ \r
        _at u3 _first (\s2 Option.map (\pf _pf _n9 (△ r pf))
            (_at s2 selfp s2 depth (△ _n9 path) true asms (△ (_resx r) e)))
          (_rgen_sitesx r s))
        (Bool.and (List.is_empty asms)
          (Bool.and (List.is_empty (_stars e)) (Bool.not (_has_resx e))))) u2)
    (\pf \u2 Option.some pf)
    (_stg_split selfp depth path asms e s blocked) △

_stg_read = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s \blocked
  triage
    ((Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.some (_pf Snat.zero △)) (List.is_empty e)) △)
    (\n (Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.some (_pf Snat.one n))
      (Bool.or (_spec_eq e [_val n]) (_spec_eq e [_resx n]))) △)
    (\f \x (triage
      (\u2 Option.match
        (\u3 _at u3 _stg_split2 selfp depth path asms e s blocked)
        (\e2 \u3 Option.map (_pf Snat.two) (_at u3 selfp x depth (△ _n6 (△ _n6 path)) true asms e2))
        (_remove _one e) u2)
      (\g \u2 _at u2 _stg_split2 selfp depth path asms e s blocked)
      (\ff \fx \u2 (triage (\u3 Option.none)
        (\g2 \u3 _at u3 _stg_split2 selfp depth path asms e s blocked)
        (\g2 \g3 \u3 _at u3 _stg_split2 selfp depth path asms e s blocked) ff) u2)
      f) △)
    s

# The full normal form is tried on a small budget and the head normal form is
# the fallback on the big one. A lazy machine's states have no normal form at
# all — the recursion unfolds forever under the constructor it emits — so
# every full attempt on one is spent to exhaustion, and the attempt being
# cheap is what keeps this prover's costs at reading pace. Successful
# normalizations across every program certified here stay under 800 steps.
_nf_budget = Snat.from_nat 2000
_lazilyx = \q (Option.match
  (\u _at u Quoted.head_normalize _head_budget q)
  (\r \_ Option.some r)
  (Quoted.normalize_lazy _nf_budget q)) △

# GEN-TREE, ported from the eager prover: a subterm a hypothesis proves
# evaluates to a known-size chain — part sizes stacked over a residual —
# becomes a fresh tree variable, its parts recorded in its name for
# [_foldx]'s widened measure; the stem-up attempt and the 1 it returns to
# the spec are the eager rule's. Two lazy differences. The instance match
# runs on both sides' own normal forms: a whnf state leaves its guts at
# whatever stage the budget reached, so hypothesis and candidate spellings
# agree only once each is normalized alone — and on the variable-to-variable
# instances the rule wants, the two standalone reductions are isomorphic and
# truncate at the same places. And the rule is gated to goals owing a ⟨r⟩
# against a hypothesis owing one: without RGEN's residual there is no chain
# judgment to instantiate — which also keeps it out of every phase, since a
# spec never carries both tails.
_norm_t = \q Option.map Pair.fst (_lazilyx q)
_resvarx = _atomx Option.none (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none) Option.some
_foldxn = \a \t Pair.let a $ \state \r Pair.let r $ \spec \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \v \hid
  (Bool.match (\u
    Option.bind (\sN Option.bind (\tN
      Option.bind (\s Option.bind
        (\w Bool.match Option.none
          (Option.sequence $ List.map (_renamex s) (_core spec))
          (_below v w))
        (_image s v))
        (_match sN tN []))
      (_at sN _norm_t t)) (_at u _norm_t state))
    (\u Option.none)
    (List.any _is_star spec)) △
_stg_gentree = \selfp \depth \path \asms \e \s
  (Bool.match (\u2 Option.none) (\u2
    _at u2 _first (\c _first (\a
      let (\k1s \fopt Option.bind (\f
            Option.bind (\b
              let (List.filter (\at Option.match true (\_ false) (_resvarx at)) f) $ \core2
              Option.bind (\parts
                Option.bind (\rest
                  Option.bind (\rest2
                    let (_gname (List.concat parts [b])) $ \gn
                    Option.map (\sub _pf _n10 (△ (△ gn c) sub))
                      (_at rest2 selfp (_replace c (_var gn) s) depth (△ _n10 path) true asms
                        (△ (_sz gn) (List.concat k1s rest2))))
                  (_remove (_sz b) rest))
                (_minus core2 e))
              (Option.sequence $ List.map
                (_atomx Option.none Option.some (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.none)) core2))
            (List.foldr (\at \acc Option.alt (_resvarx at) acc) Option.none f))
          fopt) $ \attempt
      Option.match (\u3 _at u3 attempt [_one] (_at u3 _foldxn a (_app △ c))) (\pf \u3 Option.some pf)
        (attempt [] (_foldxn a c)) △)
      asms) (_subterms s))
    (Bool.and (_has_resx e)
      (Bool.and (List.is_empty (_stars e))
        (List.any (\a2 Pair.let a2 $ \st2 \r5 Pair.let r5 $ \sp2 \_ _has_resx sp2) asms)))) △

# REL-FOLD, under the lazy judgment: the same shared [_rel], on this
# prover's reduction with a smaller full-form budget — a REL state that has
# a normal form reaches it fast or not at all, and the __wn states never
# have one, so the big budget only made every attempt that must fail pay
# full price first. Star- and residual-free goals against star- and
# residual-free hypotheses only, so neither tail's semantics is ever read
# by REL — nor misread: the shared renamer speaks the eager prover's four
# atoms, and this judgment's ⟨★⟩ and ⟨r⟩ are not among them.
_rel_nfb = Snat.from_nat 300
_rel_lazily = \q (Option.match
  (\u _at u Quoted.head_normalize _head_budget q)
  (\r \_ Option.some r)
  (Quoted.normalize_lazy _rel_nfb q)) △
_stg_relfold = \q \asms \e
  (Bool.match (\u2 Option.none) (\u2
    _at u2 _first (\a Pair.let a $ \hst \r Pair.let r $ \spec \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \v \hid
      (Bool.match (\u3 Option.none) (\u3
        Option.map (Pair.match $ \w \sub _pf _n11 (△ w sub))
          (_at u3 _rel_try1 _rel_lazily true q e hst spec v))
        (Bool.and (List.is_empty (_stars spec)) (Bool.not (_has_resx spec)))) △)
      asms)
    (Bool.and (List.is_empty (_stars e)) (Bool.not (_has_resx e)))) △

_depthx = Snat.from_nat 5
_sizecap = 20000
_provex = fix $ \selfp \q \depth \path \ca \asms \e
  Option.match (\_ Option.none) (Pair.match $ \s \blocked \selfp
  (Bool.match (\_ \_ Option.none) (\_ \selfp
  let (List.foldr (\at \acc Option.alt (_star_name at) acc) Option.none e) $ \gstar
  let (\u5 _try u5
    [ \u6 _at u6 _stg_gentree selfp depth path asms e s
    ; \u6 _at u6 _stg_star e s
    ; \u6 _at u6 _stg_relfold q asms e
    ; \u6 _at u6 _stg_cut selfp depth path asms e s blocked
    ; \u6 _at u6 _stg_abs selfp depth path ca asms e s
    ; \u6 _at u6 _stg_read selfp depth path asms e s blocked
    ]) $ \rest
  Option.match
    (\selfp2 (Bool.match
      (\selfp3 Option.match
        (\selfp4 rest selfp4)
        (\gen \selfp4 Pair.let gen $ \s2 \r Pair.let r $ \e2 \c
          Option.map (\sub _pf _n5 (△ (△ (_genname path) c) sub))
            (_at selfp4 selfp3 s2 depth (△ _n5 path) true asms e2))
        (_at selfp3 _generalizex (_genname path) asms e s)
        selfp3)
      (\selfp3 rest selfp3)
      (List.is_empty asms)) selfp2)
    (\pf \_ Option.some pf)
    (_stg_fold gstar asms e s)
    selfp)
  (Nat.is_lte (size s) _sizecap) △ selfp))
  (_lazilyx q) selfp

# ── The borrow check ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A fold that bridged two tails borrowed its hypothesis's end states for a
# different continuation. That is sound exactly when those end states — the
# ones of the hypothesis's own split subtree, under the fold's substitution —
# also satisfy the borrowing cut's spec. Walk the finished proof, collect the
# borrow graph, prove the extra obligations, and iterate on any new borrows
# those proofs introduce.
_walk_cuts = fix $ \self \p _pf_case p (\_ []) (\_ []) self
  (Pair.match $ \_ \kids List.concat_list (List.map self kids))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \info Pair.match $ \phase \obls
    △ info (List.concat (self phase) (List.concat_list (List.map self obls))))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (\_ [])
_walk_splits = fix $ \self \p _pf_case p (\_ []) (\_ []) self
  (Pair.match $ \vp \kids △ (△ (Pair.snd vp) (_pf _n3 (△ vp kids)))
    (List.concat_list (List.map self kids)))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ Pair.match $ \phase \obls
    List.concat (self phase) (List.concat_list (List.map self obls)))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (\_ [])
_walk_borrows = fix $ \self \p _pf_case p (\_ []) (\_ []) self
  (Pair.match $ \_ \kids List.concat_list (List.map self kids))
  (Option.match [] (\c [c]))
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ Pair.match $ \phase \obls
    List.concat (self phase) (List.concat_list (List.map self obls)))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (Pair.match $ \_ self)
  (\_ [])

_validate = \proof
  let (_walk_cuts proof) $ \cuts
  let (_walk_splits proof) $ \splits
  _all (Pair.match $ \hs \r Pair.let r $ \gs \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \sigma \hid
    Option.match false (Pair.match $ \cutspec \asms
      Option.match false (\tree
        _all (\es Option.match false (\sub List.is_empty (_walk_borrows sub))
          (_provex (Quoted.apply_record sigma es) _depthx (△ _n8 (△ _n8 hid)) true asms cutspec))
          (_dedupe (_ends hs tree)))
        (List.lookup hid splits))
      (List.lookup gs cuts))
    (_walk_borrows proof)

# ── Rendering ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A certificate as one rule per line, children indented under their rule. A
# tree variable prints as its position in the input — t is the input, t01
# the right part of its left part — because that is what its name is. A
# generated name — g for a generalized count, j for abstracted junk, k for
# a tail's continuation — is unique by carrying its proof path, which reads
# as digit noise, so the renderer numbers them by first appearance instead:
# g1, j2, k3.

# The names a proof mentions, in the order the renderer prints them.
_names_in = fix $ \self \p _pf_case p
  (\_ [])
  (\n [n])
  self
  (Pair.match $ \_ \kids List.concat_list (List.map self kids))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \nc \sub Pair.let nc $ \nm \_ △ nm (self sub))
  (Pair.match $ \subst \sub List.concat (List.map Pair.fst subst) (self sub))
  (Pair.match $ \info Pair.match $ \phase \obls Pair.let info $ \st \r
    List.concat
      (List.foldr (\a \acc Option.match acc (\w △ w acc) (Option.alt (_atom_var a) (_star_name a)))
        [] (Pair.fst r))
      (List.concat (self phase) (List.concat_list (List.map self obls))))
  (\_ [])
  (Pair.match $ \r \sub △ r (self sub))
  (Pair.match $ \nc \sub Pair.let nc $ \gn \_ △ gn (self sub))
  (\_ [])

# Assign the generated names their display names, a counter per kind. A
# minted GEN-TREE name leads with a fork where every other kind leads with
# a Snat, so the fork case numbers it under its own counter.
_num_step = \env \cg \cj \ck \cr \cG \n
  let (△ env (△ cg (△ cj (△ ck (△ cr cG))))) $ \same
  List.match same (\hd \tl
    (triage
      (\u2 same)
      (\c2 Bool.match
        (\u2 Snat.match same (\h2 Snat.match same (\h3
          Snat.match (△ (△ (△ n (List.concat "g" (Nat.to_source cg))) env) (△ (Nat.add cg 1) (△ cj (△ ck (△ cr cG)))))
          (\h4 Snat.match (△ (△ (△ n (List.concat "j" (Nat.to_source cj))) env) (△ cg (△ (Nat.add cj 1) (△ ck (△ cr cG)))))
          (\h5 Snat.match (△ (△ (△ n (List.concat "k" (Nat.to_source ck))) env) (△ cg (△ cj (△ (Nat.add ck 1) (△ cr cG)))))
          (\_ △ (△ (△ n (List.concat "r" (Nat.to_source cr))) env) (△ cg (△ cj (△ ck (△ (Nat.add cr 1) cG))))) h5) h4) h3) h2) hd)
        (\u2 same)
        (Snat.is_lt hd Snat.two))
      (\a2 \b2 \u2 △ (△ (△ n (List.concat "G" (Nat.to_source cG))) env) (△ cg (△ cj (△ ck (△ cr (Nat.add cG 1))))))
      hd) △) n
_number_names = \names Pair.fst $ List.foldl (\acc \n Pair.let acc $ \env \cnt
    Pair.let cnt $ \cg \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \cj \r3 Pair.let r3 $ \ck \r4 Pair.let r4 $ \cr \cG
    Option.match (_num_step env cg cj ck cr cG n) (\_ acc) (List.lookup n env))
  (△ [] (△ 1 (△ 1 (△ 1 (△ 1 1))))) names

_render_name = \env \n Option.match
  (List.match "t" (\hd \tl
    (triage
      (List.concat "t" (List.concat_list (List.map Snat.to_string
        (List.match [] (\h2 \t2 t2) (List.reverse n)))))
      (\_ (Bool.match
        (\_ List.concat
          (Snat.match "?" (\h2 Snat.match "?" (\h3 Snat.match "g"
            (\h4 Snat.match "j" (\h5 Snat.match "k" (\_ "r") h5) h4) h3) h2) hd)
          (List.concat_list (List.map Snat.to_string (List.reverse tl))))
        (\_ List.concat "t" (List.concat_list (List.map Snat.to_string
          (List.match [] (\h2 \t2 t2) (List.reverse n)))))
        (Snat.is_lt hd Snat.two)) △)
      (\_ \_ "G")
      hd)) n)
  id
  (List.lookup n env)
_render_atom = \env _atomx "1"
  (\v List.concat "|" (List.concat (_render_name env v) "|"))
  (_render_name env)
  (\k List.concat "*" (_render_name env k))
  (\r List.concat "<" (List.concat (_render_name env r) ">"))
_render_spec = \env \e List.concat "["
  (List.concat (List.join "," (List.map (_render_atom env) e)) "]")

# A REL derivation, one co-reduction rule per line: SAME both sides met,
# FOLD a pair hypothesis closed an instance, CASE a split of the variable
# the sides wait on, USE the machine collapsed at its own continuation (its
# obligation first, its continuation after), IH an obligation closed by the
# anchor induction.
_render_rel = \env fix $ \self \ind \p Pair.let p $ \tag \pay
  let (List.concat "  " ind) $ \ind2
  (Snat.match (\_ [List.concat ind "SAME"])
   (\t1 Snat.match (\_ [List.concat ind "FOLD"])
   (\t2 Snat.match (Pair.match $ \v \kids
       △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "CASE " (_render_name env v)))
         (List.concat_list (List.map (self ind2) kids)))
   (\t3 Snat.match (Pair.match $ \x \r Pair.let r $ \obl \cont
       △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "USE " (_render_name env x)))
         (List.concat (self ind2 obl) (self ind2 cont)))
   (\t4 Snat.match (\_ [List.concat ind "IH"])
   (\t5 Snat.match (Pair.match $ \x \r Pair.let r $ \obl \cont
       △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "USEP " (_render_name env x)))
         (List.concat (self ind2 obl) (self ind2 cont)))
   (\t6 Snat.match (Pair.match $ \x \r Pair.let r $ \obl \cont
       △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "USEPW " (_render_name env x)))
         (List.concat (self ind2 obl) (self ind2 cont)))
   (\t7 Pair.match $ \x \r Pair.let r $ \ol \r2 Pair.let r2 $ \og \cont
       △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "USEP2 " (_render_name env x)))
         (List.concat (self ind2 ol) (List.concat (self ind2 og) (self ind2 cont))))
   t6) t5) t4) t3) t2) t1) tag) pay

# render pf — the proof tree, one rule per line, indented by depth. Each node
# contributes its list of lines, prefixed by the indentation it was handed;
# a child gets two more spaces.
render = \pf let (_number_names (_names_in pf)) $ \env
  List.join "\n" $ (fix $ \self \ind \p
  let (List.concat "  " ind) $ \ind2
  _pf_case p
  (\_ [List.concat ind "ZERO"])
  (\n [List.concat ind (List.concat "VALUE " (_render_name env n))])
  (\sub △ (List.concat ind "PEEL") (self ind2 sub))
  (Pair.match $ \vp \kids Pair.let vp $ \v \_
    △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "SPLIT " (_render_name env v)))
      (List.concat_list (List.map (self ind2) kids)))
  (Option.match [List.concat ind "FOLD"] (\_ [List.concat ind "FOLD*"]))
  (Pair.match $ \nc \sub Pair.let nc $ \nm \_
    △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "GEN " (_render_name env nm))) (self ind2 sub))
  (Pair.match $ \subst \sub
    △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "ABSTRACT "
        (List.join "," (List.map (Pair.match $ \nm \_ _render_name env nm) subst))))
      (self ind2 sub))
  (Pair.match $ \info Pair.match $ \phase \obls Pair.let info $ \st \r
    △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "CUT " (_render_spec env (Pair.fst r))))
      (List.concat (self ind2 phase) (List.concat_list (List.map (self ind2) obls))))
  (Pair.match $ \st \state [List.concat ind "END"])
  (Pair.match $ \r \sub △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "RGEN " (_render_name env r))) (self ind2 sub))
  (Pair.match $ \nc \sub Pair.let nc $ \gn \_
    △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "GEN-TREE " (_render_name env gn))) (self ind2 sub))
  (Pair.match $ \w \sub
    △ (List.concat ind (List.concat "REL " (_render_name env w)))
      (_render_rel env ind2 sub))) "" pf

# certify_size p — the proof that p returns its argument's node count, as an
# Snat, for every tree, under normal-order evaluation; or none.
certify_size = \p
  Option.bind (\pf Bool.match (\_ Option.none) (\_ Option.some pf) (_validate pf) △)
    (_provex (_app (Reflect.quote p) (_var _input)) _depthx [Snat.one] true [] [_sz _input])

# computes_size p — true only if p returns the node count of its argument, as
# an Snat, for every tree. False means "not certifiable here", not "not size".
computes_size = \p Option.match false (\_ true) (certify_size p)



